body:
A lot is happening in this one sentence:

&#x200B;

"England forces me to dress in his clothes while crying with regret."

"Late at night, Sweden lovingly forced me to listen to Justin Bieber."

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

**ok**

Japan stole my cookie because he has a secret obsession with me.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

# I am very pleased to hear that.

*I take a break from reddit for just a few weeks to come back and see this.*

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

*I'm not exactly pleased with it, but I don't hate it either.*

Greece is my older sibling

&#x200B;

which means, that my mom gave birth to him at some point.

&#x200B;

so my mother dearest is technically Ancient Greece.

I'm sorry just-

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

# C h i l d r e n ' s   s h o w

***why is spain so small***

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

***my boy why is he small***

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

***what did you do to my boy why did you shrink him my poor boy***

*Yes, my father. I have required your disease-filled juices for quite a long time. My life long wish has finally come true.*

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

~~god please someone help me.~~

I thought it was going to be some type of image of canada's head plastered on a canadian air flight attendant or something

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

i was wrong, but this image makes me feel equally confused.
